      ],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "Bitcoin priced in gold peaked in late 2024, so similar to 2021 one can argue that the real Bitcoin peak may have been December 2024 when measured in another hard money.",
      "certainty": "speculative",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "So any thoughts on where you think the industry is going? From a digital credit and treasury company perspective. Yeah, I mean, I think, like I said, we've only seen digital credit really and mostly a Bitcoin bear market. Like, I believe Stretch came out in like June or July of last year, 2025. Strategy, like their stock, for instance, peaked in late 2024."
    },
    {
      "label": "f91c4a6b4a5ea9388c32",
      "speaker_changes_inside": "no",
      "view": "own_sincere",
      "referents": [
        {
          "word": "that",
          "refers_to": "Achilles heel with Bitcoin",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        }
      ],
      "conditions": [
        {
          "text": "especially now with all these things happening with AI, quantum",
          "inside": true
        }
      ],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "Self-custody is turning into something people are increasingly scared of and this is the Achilles heel with Bitcoin especially now with AI and quantum developments.",
      "certainty": "likely",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "But gold got centralized because of its physicality, largely, right? I mean, it's difficult to transport and verify."
    },
    {
      "label": "04a149678014424229d3",
      "speaker_changes_inside": "no",
      "view": "hypothetical",
      "referents": [
        {
          "word": "that",
          "refers_to": "somebody makes a loan in Bitcoin",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        },
        {
          "word": "they",
          "refers_to": "somebody else is going to deposit in another bank",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        },
        {
          "word": "it",
          "refers_to": "money",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        }
      ],
      "conditions": [
        {
          "text": "if somebody makes a loan in Bitcoin",
          "inside": true
        }
      ],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "On a Bitcoin standard if somebody makes a loan in Bitcoin that creates a deposit leading to credit creation where money is created and denominated in something else.",
      "certainty": "certain",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "Pavlina, a question for you then about the idea of increasing money and about sovereignty, which you brought up earlier, and you brought up as well, global sovereignty as well, the ability for countries to issue their own currencies, to control their own currencies. Can this happen? while at the same time they don't have the power to increase the amount of money that is in circulation. Is there a way to create a fiat system without also increasing money? I'm not so sure that I understand the question. The money is created when we finance economic activity. And so you can have money that is privately created. You can have Bitcoin, and money will be created."
    },
    {
      "label": "316f66f81603ea55899a",
      "speaker_changes_inside": "no",
      "view": "own_sincere",
      "referents": [
        {
          "word": "it",
          "refers_to": "price of Bitcoin going higher",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        },
        {
          "word": "it",
          "refers_to": "creating more dollar credit against Bitcoin to acquire more Bitcoin",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "yes"
        }
      ],
      "conditions": [
        {
          "text": "if the price of Bitcoin goes higher",
          "inside": true
        }
      ],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "If Bitcoin's price goes higher it becomes better collateral for issuing more dollar credit and this could be sustainable because Bitcoin is perfectly scarce while more dollars are constantly created by design in the financial system.",
      "certainty": "speculative",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "Or like, what do you, what do you, is there a specific like point of why you think that would happen? Yeah. I mean, I think part of it is like just the simple failure of fiat currencies."
    },
    {
      "label": "43e6d312e1a1e6a4e33c",
      "speaker_changes_inside": "no",
      "view": "own_sincere",
      "referents": [],
      "conditions": [
        {
          "text": "if you want to have confidence that any purchases of Bitcoin are going to be legal",
          "inside": true
        }
      ],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "Authorization from Congress is needed to have confidence that any administration purchases of Bitcoin are legal.",
      "certainty": "certain",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "I can tell you the president's interested in it. I can tell you that there's been a lot of discussion about how we might be able to do that."
    },
    {
      "label": "f81db985a39acf8dcc8e",
      "speaker_changes_inside": "no",
      "view": "hypothetical",
      "referents": [],
      "conditions": [
        {
          "text": "in the past cycle",
          "inside": true
        },
        {
          "text": "if the treasury companies didn't exist",
          "inside": true
        }
      ],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "If treasury companies had not existed in the past cycle the Bitcoin bull market maybe would have been higher though it is hard to tell.",
      "certainty": "speculative",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "Although I hear I'm thinking our friend Parker Lewis might say, well, hang on, if these, you know, if these common stocks are at a premium, then, you know, let's say, just for example, say, let's say you're at 1.5xMNAV or 2xM nav. He would say he might argue to us that, hey, that customer or that person who has bought the common stock is paying double the price or 1.5x the price when in his mind, it would have all just otherwise gone directly to Bitcoin, right? I mean, I think like in the past cycle,"
    },
    {
      "label": "0c751a33022013fb3086",
      "speaker_changes_inside": "no",
      "view": "own_sincere",
      "referents": [
        {
          "word": "it",
          "refers_to": "Bitcoin",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        },
        {
          "word": "that",
          "refers_to": "why the price got high and got low",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        }
      ],
      "conditions": [],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "Everyone loves Bitcoin and wants exposure when it is rising in a super hot bull market but hates it and avoids exposure when it is falling in a bear market and that is why its price gets high at the top and low at the bottom.",
      "certainty": "likely",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "Like, if Bitcoin falls 50%, you're like, what were you doing for the last year? Like, that was terrible. And so, like, you have, if you were obtaining exposure to Bitcoin, whether it's for a company, financial advisor, or an individual, you have to have that longer time horizon."
    },
    {
      "label": "6353ef6c32236e89f0cc",
      "speaker_changes_inside": "no",
      "view": "own_sincere",
      "referents": [
        {
          "word": "that",
          "refers_to": "the instability from the market system and mode of production",
          "inside": true,
          "changes_assertion": "no"
        }
      ],
      "conditions": [
        {
          "text": "even if you have Bitcoin as a standard",
          "inside": true
        }
      ],
      "retraction": "none",
      "time_ok": "yes",
      "proposition": "Even with Bitcoin as a standard you will not prevent speculators from issuing liabilities denominated in Bitcoin because there will always be somebody issuing some kind of loan.",
      "certainty": "certain",
      "speaker_is": "guest",
      "speaker_evidence": "Look, I'm not defending wars or governments bailing out banks. I have written about this, explicitly opposed this. My focus has always been on the real economy. And there is a confusion. It's not money that finances the war. It's people. It is the resources. It's who's fighting the wars. It is who's producing. It is the base, the material base that actually, instead of producing things that we all need, We're developing bombs. That is the issue. To me, the question of technology is not the specific technology, but it's a question of monetary design, like institutional design. And it's a question of governance of law. It is a question of law. It is not a question of the specific thing that is being used. Have no illusion that wars are going to stop because there's Bitcoin. I expect that far more exploitation is going to happen if that very scarce resource is somehow the only thing we use to pay for things. I find I expect far more deflation, defaults. The way the economy works, we can just start from some hypothetical, I consider this scenario to be the unicorn scenario. Like we have to start from here to there. Like we need to figure out how from this system we get to a more democratic system. And the Bitcoin is priced in. in dollars. It is priced in already existing currencies. You don't simply just disappear the current monetary system."
    }
  ]
